From 37967a3d2ed1adcb1ceb03ea87dc8cae019a9526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Hao <49104178+VinceHow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:51:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Painted look: meet the team as the first-open meet card;
 the name tag's rough states
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Meet the team: each teammate's wave clip in a rounded inked frame on their crayon, beside an ink-paper card in their
colour: name big, role and the agent mark small, the line in their voice, what they bring, the count. painted.js drops
a muted, looping <video> into the face slot (the portrait is its poster and the fallback); the blurred studio door is
behind it, as behind her name tag. Adds the five portraits and wave clips to cast/intro/.
Name tag: data-state rough is a little sketchier (lighter ink, a dashed rule) and settles to full ink when shown;
the status line polishing · slow · rough is plain, with a small ink stroke while the team polishes. Hooks only.
